THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
--------------------

This work is a weight format and a set of kernels for llama.cpp / ggml, which
are distributed under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-2024 The ggml authors.
MIT-licensed material may be incorporated into an Apache-2.0 work; the
attribution requirement below satisfies its terms.

Three files reproduce or adapt upstream code and say so in their own headers:

  benchmarks/i2s_tiled.h
      Reproduces the ARITHMETIC of tinyBLAS_I2S_AVX::gemm from
      ggml/src/ggml-cpu/llamafile/sgemm.cpp -- the same 2-bit unpack and the
      same vpmaddubsw sequence -- so that this project's format can be compared
      against the shape llama.cpp actually runs. Register allocation differs and
      the file explains why.

  src/ggml_t5b_glue.c, src/ggml_t5b_glue.h
      Implement the ggml-facing contract of the i2_s kernels: the same
      signatures, the same sum(code*a) return convention, and the same
      downstream post-processing (dot - act_sums[j]) * scale. The contract is
      upstream's; the implementation is this project's.

  tools/gguf_inspect.py
      Parses the GGUF container format defined by ggml.

No upstream source file is redistributed verbatim in this repository. The
integration itself is applied as a patch to an unmodified llama.cpp checkout and
is not included here.

MODEL WEIGHTS
